# General Conventions

## Language & Type Safety

- Always use TypeScript for all code files
- Prefer explicit types over `any` - use `unknown` when type is truly unknown

```typescript
// Prefer: (value: unknown) => ...
// Avoid: (value: any) => ...
```

## Files & Folders

- Use kebab-case for all folders and files (e.g., `user-profile.tsx`, `payment-logs/`)
- Keep files small and focused on single responsibility
- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) for clean imports; avoid deep barrel re-exports that pull in large trees (risk of cycles and slower resolution)

## Variables & Functions

- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and object properties
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants and enums
- Use descriptive names that clearly indicate purpose

## Imports and Exports

- Group imports in this order: external libraries, internal modules, relative imports
- Use absolute imports with `@/` prefix for project code under `src/` (the configured path)
- Sort imports alphabetically within each group
- Use named imports over default imports when possible
- Remove unused imports

```typescript
import { z } from "zod"

import { apiClient } from "@/lib/api-client"

import { LocalHelper } from "./local-helper"
```

## Environment & Configuration

- Use environment variables for all configuration and sensitive values
- Never commit sensitive data to version control

## Code Comments & Documentation

- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- Add comments only for non-obvious business logic, workarounds, or non-obvious "why" (not "what")
